Falsifies `system_tests::user::running_space_tests::a_bound_space_dies_with_its_thread_not_with_its_capabilities`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect: the reaper stops taking a dead thread's space out of the registry. The registry owns
every space since §249 (a running address space stays nameable), so a thread no longer drops its
space by dying, and without this take a dead process's space stays named, with its root, its ASID
and its revocation records held, for the life of the machine.

Expected to fail: the assertion after the reader is reaped, that the space is gone.

